message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite the repository and the accompanying paper."
type: software
title: "RailGuard: Railway Wheel-Flat Vibration Simulation and Feature Analysis"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-05
authors:
  - family-names: Nadyr
    given-names: Valiollakh
    affiliation: "Nazarbayev Intellectual School of Science and Mathematics, Nauryzbay District, Almaty, Kazakhstan"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - railway wheel flat
  - vibration analysis
  - Hertzian contact
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - condition monitoring
  - PyWavelets
abstract: >-
  RailGuard is a reproducible simulation-only study of railway wheel-flat
  vibration using a two-degree-of-freedom wheel-bogie model, Monte Carlo
  parameter variation, and time-, frequency-, and time-frequency-domain
  features.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "RailGuard: Physics-Based Simulation and Experimental Design for Railway Wheel-Flat Detection Using Vibration Analysis"
